soma verify app.cell → ✓ entering Hub.done while Worker.armed ; soma run --fresh app.cell ; soma run app.cell Hub.finish x ; soma run app.cell Hub.hst x → done ; soma run app.cell → "Worker x: idle". Hub.finish does `emit flip(k)` (its interior Worker arms) then enters done. The product search delivers the emit by the one rule (product.rs:994-1011) — but the program is started by `soma run app.cell Hub.finish` (also `soma test`, `soma serve`), which does not start interior cells (commands/run.rs: plain interpreter; STRUCTURE_DESIGN §4 admits serve/test): the listener does not run, and the `while` rule the proof ticked is broken. The model makes a listener run ALWAYS; the run may not run it — not an over-approximation.
